{
  "anomaly_detected": true,
  "confidence": 0.85,
  "anomalies": [
    {
      "category": "short_to_supply",
      "components": ["U6"],
      "pins": ["U6.6"],
      "nets": ["+3V3"],
      "observed": "U6 pin 6, named VCP (charge-pump output), is connected directly to the +3V3 power net. The other two identical TMC2209 drivers, U5 and U7, have a 100 nF capacitor on their VCP pins (C49 on /VCP_{pH}, C51 on /VCP_{NB}); U6 has no corresponding VCP capacitor.",
      "expected": "A TMC2209 VCP pin should be connected to its required charge-pump capacitor, not shorted to a logic supply rail. U6 should be wired like U5/U7 with a VCP capacitor and should not appear on the +3V3 net.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "source": "netlist",
          "quote": "(node (ref \"U6\") (pin \"6\") (pinfunction \"VCP\") (pintype \"output\"))"
        },
        {
          "source": "netlist",
          "quote": "(net (code \"61\") (name \"/VCP_{pH}\") (class \"Isolated,Default\")\n      (node (ref \"C49\") (pin \"1\") (pintype \"passive\"))\n      (node (ref \"U5\") (pin \"6\") (pinfunction \"VCP\") (pintype \"output\")))"
        }
      ],
      "impact": "The Nutrient-A stepper driver U6 will not have a proper charge-pump supply; its gate drivers are likely to fail to switch, and the shorted charge-pump output may load or damage U6/the 3.3 V rail, causing loss of Nutrient-A dosing.",
      "confidence": 0.85
    }
  ],
  "summary": "The design files show a clear anomaly: U6's TMC2209 VCP charge-pump pin is tied directly to +3V3, unlike U5/U7 which have VCP capacitors, likely disabling or damaging the Nutrient-A pump driver."
}

